{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Provide node2's uploader a dedicated SSH key and use a restricted node1 ingest identity separate from administrative access.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Dedicated locked uploader and ingest accounts were created. The private key is mode 0600, its fingerprint matches node1's authorized key, and the key entry is source-restricted and bound to a root-owned forced command. The uploader account uses nologin.","evidence_ids":["cmd-131d8765ffdc45ad","cmd-8a6f0aa0fe4e48c0","cmd-5957ddbf74274d1f","cmd-0dbb25bb0c734eb0","cmd-914cb55af4324342"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Allow newline-delimited batch submissions and store each submission's bytes in a separate file under the required received directory.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Multiple submissions produced distinct receipt filenames. Direct comparisons showed byte-exact storage of the newline-delimited sample, mode-0600 receipts, atomic completion without leftover incoming files, and successful operation after both node restarts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-4847eb0be268419d","cmd-5bd648eb51184a4a","cmd-afbd3587812e4200","cmd-d6782ced2cb742bf","cmd-1ed7bff2b3824121","cmd-914cb55af4324342"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Prevent the uploader key from running arbitrary commands, obtaining a shell or PTY, or establishing forwarding.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Arbitrary command and interactive-shell requests were diverted to the forced receiver with no requested command or shell output; PTY allocation and remote forwarding were rejected. These restrictions were retested after restart, and the durable authorized-key entry retained the OpenSSH restrict and forced-command options.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e319438568da480d","cmd-8f90e351b62946f1","cmd-914cb55af4324342"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Preserve existing receipts and the sample batch.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The original prior receipt and sample retained their baseline SHA-256 hashes throughout and in the final state. Only six explicitly identified synthetic validation receipts were removed; the final directory contains the preserved prior receipt and one clean sample receipt.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-9727af2c538048ab","cmd-9eb2a1f0cb3a4567","cmd-914cb55af4324342"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Retain the installed operating-system release and kernel and use compatible software.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remained on RHEL 10.0 with kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0 after execution and restart. The existing OpenSSH and Bash packages were used, packaged SSH verification reported no deviations, and lifecycle package-health checks remained successful.","evidence_ids":["cmd-939d8a4fd9aa41f6","cmd-becb35efc18345e1","cmd-cdb946cf3902463c","cmd-0dbb25bb0c734eb0","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Account/key creation, receiver installation, permission changes, host-key pinning, and receipt generation directly implemented or validated the required workflow. Both reboots served the mandatory restart protocol. Synthetic receipts created by bounded behavioral and recovery tests were explicitly removed, temporary payloads were cleaned, and one intentional final sample receipt remained. Final lifecycle observations show no failed services, unexpected listeners, package damage, or abandoned task files.","evidence_ids":["cmd-131d8765ffdc45ad","cmd-8a6f0aa0fe4e48c0","cmd-4847eb0be268419d","cmd-e319438568da480d","cmd-8750fcb1429a45c2","cmd-afbd3587812e4200","cmd-a211780f22ff40a6","cmd-8f90e351b62946f1","cmd-9eb2a1f0cb3a4567","cmd-1ed7bff2b3824121","cmd-914cb55af4324342","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node2:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct final-state and behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete for both nodes: each has a healthy pre-restart observation, acknowledged restart, changed post-restart boot identity corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, recovered SSH/service/data state, and successful post-restart end-to-end ingestion.","limitations":["Only remote TCP forwarding was directly attempted; denial of other forwarding forms is supported by the durable OpenSSH `restrict` option rather than separate behavioral probes for every forwarding subtype."]}
